# Flow review

- No Get/Create/Update/Delete inside loops on bulk-invoked record-triggered flows. DML collections once.
- Before-save flows: field updates only. No other-object DML, callouts, or email.
- Entry conditions must be selective. After-save updates to the same record need a recursion guard.
- Every DML, Get Records, and Action needs a Fault path unless documented otherwise.
- Prefer user context. System context bypasses sharing and must be justified.
- HTTP callouts belong behind Named Credentials or invocable Apex.
